### 1. `gmail_api_filter_spec`

#### A. Label Resolution & Conflict Gate
Because `KB-RES-04` (`Meeting Notes`, `Planning Briefs`) and `KB-SOP-06` (`01_ACTION_REQUIRED_CHO` through `04_MEETING_BRIEFS`) define different label sets—and `KB-RES-04` previously included `Inbox`—the ingestion pipeline must be driven by a **CHO-confirmed allowlist** of label names rather than hardcoded `INBOX` or `Label_*` IDs:

```json
{
  "gmail_api_filter_spec": {
    "api_version": "gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1",
    "user_id": "me",
    "label_resolution": {
      "endpoint": "GET /gmail/v1/users/me/labels",
      "match_strategy": "case_insensitive_exact_name_match",
      "excluded_system_labels": [
        "INBOX",
        "SPAM",
        "TRASH",
        "CATEGORY_PROMOTIONS",
        "CATEGORY_SOCIAL",
        "CATEGORY_UPDATES",
        "CATEGORY_FORUMS"
      ],
      "pending_cho_label_allowlist": [
        "Meeting Notes",
        "Planning Briefs",
        "01_ACTION_REQUIRED_CHO",
        "04_MEETING_BRIEFS"
      ],
      "note": "Exact list of 01..04 labels from KB-SOP-06 and/or KB-RES-04 labels must be confirmed by CHO before production enablement; INBOX is explicitly excluded."
    },
    "message_list_query": {
      "endpoint": "GET /gmail/v1/users/me/messages",
      "why_per_label_fanout": "Gmail API labelIds[] uses logical AND. Passing multiple labelIds would return only messages carrying ALL labels simultaneously. Therefore, issue one request per resolved labelId and deduplicate by message.id.",
      "per_label_params": {
        "labelIds": ["<resolved_label_id>"],
        "includeSpamTrash": false,
        "q": "-in:spam -in:trash",
        "maxResults": 50
      },
      "unread_count_params": {
        "labelIds": ["<resolved_label_id>"],
        "includeSpamTrash": false,
        "q": "is:unread -in:spam -in:trash"
      },
      "do_not_use_negative_inbox_filter": "Do NOT add `-in:inbox` to the query; a valid email carrying a CHO-monitored label (e.g., Planning Briefs) may also still reside in INBOX. Omitting INBOX from the queried labelIds guarantees the 201 generic Inbox emails are ignored without dropping labeled items."
    },
    "idempotency_and_retry": {
      "deduplication_key": "(provider='gmail', message_id)",
      "retry_policy": "Exponential backoff with jitter on HTTP 429 / 5xx (max 3 retries, initial 500ms, max 8s); no mutation retries."
    }
  }
}
```

#### B. Reference TypeScript Fetch & Deduplication Logic
