### 3. `oauth_scope_notes`

Per `KB-GOV-01` and `KB-RES-02` (least-privilege OAuth2 and token memory discipline):

- **Required Gmail Scope (Read-Only):**
  - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly` — Sufficient for `users.labels.list`, `users.messages.list`, and `users.messages.get` (metadata/snippet).
- **Prohibited Gmail Scopes (Must NOT be requested or enabled for ingestion):**
  - `gmail.modify`, `gmail.labels`, `mail.google.com` — Prevents any autonomous label creation/mutation, message archiving, or deletion.
  - `gmail.send` — Outbound email remains draft-only and gated on explicit CHO approval (`KB-GOV-01`).
- **Calendar Scope Boundary:**
  - `calendar.events` write scope is currently active on the Google token per Workspace telemetry, but **must remain isolated** from the Gmail ingestion worker; any calendar requests surfaced in monitored Gmail labels are routed to Daniel (Inbox & Calendar) and gated on explicit CHO confirmation (`KB-SOP-06`).
- **Token Hygiene (`KB-RES-02`):**
  - OAuth2 access tokens remain strictly in client/runtime memory and renew silently via Google Identity Services. Only non-secret briefing metadata (headers, snippet, label names, UTC timestamps) may be written to the Workspace snapshot.

