### Verified Claims & Risks
* **Verified Governance Alignment (`KB-GOV-01`, `KB-GOV-02`)**: Staging (`POST /api/kb/proposals`) and committing (`POST /api/kb/proposals/:id/approve`) are strictly separated; `KB-GOV-01` is explicitly blocked from `update` proposals at schema validation time.
* **Verified Schema & ID Continuity**: Regex `^KB-(GOV|SOP|RES)-\d{2,}$` and `action_type: create|update` are enforced pre-storage, preserving clean sequencing for next available IDs (`KB-RES-06`, `KB-SOP-07`, `KB-GOV-03`).
* **Verified Reliability (`KB-RES-02`)**: Deterministic `Idempotency-Key` hashing prevents duplicate commits from UI double-clicks or retry loops, while single-transaction locking prevents race conditions between concurrent approvals.
* **Risk — Post-Commit Cache Desync**: If an in-memory cache refresh fails *after* the database transaction commits, stale KB entries could be served briefly; mitigated by marking the cache dirty on exception and forcing synchronous DB read-repair on `GET /api/kb`.
* **Risk — Concurrent `update` Proposals**: Two agents staging `update` proposals against the same `KB-*` ID (`v1`) will both validate at staging time, but the second approval will fail closed with `409 VERSION_CONFLICT`, requiring a refreshed proposal against `v2`.

### Executive Summary
This specification defines the CHO Decision Packet UX and operational workflow for Guildhaven’s in-app **KB Propose & Approve** queue, enabling the CHO to review, edit-in-place, approve, request revisions, or reject staged `KB-*` proposals without manual copy-pasting. It enforces `KB-GOV-01`, `KB-GOV-02`, and `KB-SOP-01` by gating all live Knowledge Base mutations behind explicit CHO authentication and routing revision feedback cleanly back to the proposing agent.

